{
  "id": "ss.enemy.bristle",
  "name": "Bristle",
  "description": "The burrow's fast chaff — a silverfish out of the wall seams, and the first cut of it was a pale bug with bar legs, which is the one thing the fastest body on the roster cannot be. Redrawn as a comet: a bright wedge at the front and everything else swept behind it into hair. The bristles are the creature. Six spines fan back off the flanks at widening angles, three filaments trail past the tail, and the body between them is a narrow dart that barely reads on its own — so what you see arriving is a direction, which is exactly what this thing is. Legs rake the way legs do — front pair reaching forward, rear pair trailing back, middle straight out to the side. Drawn from directly above along +x, because the game turns it to its heading rather than flipping it, and a top-down body has no up to protect. Palest thing here on purpose: it runs on #372d3f earth and the quickest body must never be the hardest to see. Gameplay radius 7.",
